  "body": "What happens: the post-merge gate on main 0db66c44e is red. One test fails:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/winding_align.rs` :: `the_inside_out_stl_fixture_reads_inside_out_and_refuses`\n\nThe assert at winding_align.rs:189 fails: `left: [Outward]`, `right: [InsideOut]`. The checker reads the inside-out fixture as an outward body. The model import path no longer classifies that fixture. The follow-on refusal cannot fire.\n\nExpected: winding_of reports InsideOut for testdata/models/cube_inside_out.stl. lay_on_plane then refuses with a name.\n\nEvidence: run https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/43648025560 (post-merge.yml, batch tier, gate step 08, app suites). The failure is a 0.20 s functional assert, not the #1605 hang. Only test 1 of 9 in the binary failed.\n\nWindow: this is the first post-merge run that COMPLETED since 20:1xZ. Seven earlier runs (from 43644568679 on) were cancelled by later merges (cancel-in-progress). The regression entered main somewhere in 101d82f9ddb..0db66c44e24. That range holds the cut merge b8e4d8294 and the post-cut fixes #1712, #1639, #1721, #1704, #1729.\n\nFound while watching the post-merge gate (this lane).\n\nDone means: the binary passes on a green post-merge run, or the test change is explained and pinned by a follow-up.\n",
